This would fix the Love Cat and Kathleen Sinsuat cases IF their locationOfMiner is "Pinas". But I'm not 100% sure about this.

Actually, let me think about this more carefully. The user has been consistently saying items are priced in PHP. The Love Cat items and Kathleen Sinsuat are likely Philippine clients (Pinas). 

But what about "International" clients? They might be from other countries and pay in USD or other currencies.

I think the safest heuristic is: if currency is blank AND locationOfMiner is "Pinas", assume PHP. This is specific enough to not cause false positives.

Let me make this change.

